BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Santa Rosa Junior College
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260508T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260508T200000
LOCATION:Burbank Theater - Santa Rosa Campus
SUMMARY:Make it COUNT - Spring 2026 Dance Show
DESCRIPTION:Make It COUNT brings together faculty choreography\, student 
 works\, and selected solos\, duets\, and trios in a vibrant concert that 
 highlights the creativity and versatility of SRJC dancers. From mathemati
 cal patterns and sequences to personal stories tied to age\, time\, and d
 ata\, each piece offers a unique interpretation of how numbers shape our 
 world.  The concert also features guest artists bringing exciting new voi
 ces to the stage. Farrah McAdam celebrates Bruno Mars' discography throug
 h a dynamic jazz-funk set\, while Bernadette Alverio of The Movement Lab 
 explores an edgy modern piece centered around the concept of "9 lives."  
 The program showcases a range of styles including contemporary\, modern\,
  jazz\, and experimental dance\, reflecting the diverse voices within the
  department. In addition to performance\, the production emphasizes mento
 rship\, collaboration\, and professional development\, giving students ha
 nds-on experience in choreography\, rehearsal process\, and live theater 
 production.Buy tickets here! (https://www.srjcathletics.com/Athletic_Tick
 ets)
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><em>Make It COUNT</em> brings together fa
 culty choreography\, student works\, and selected solos\, duets\, and tri
 os in a vibrant concert that highlights the creativity and versatility of
  SRJC dancers. From mathematical patterns and sequences to personal stori
 es tied to age\, time\, and data\, each piece offers a unique interpretat
 ion of how numbers shape our world.</p><p>  The concert also features gue
 st artists bringing exciting new voices to the stage. Farrah McAdam celeb
 rates Bruno Mars' discography through a dynamic jazz-funk set\, while Ber
 nadette Alverio of The Movement Lab explores an edgy modern piece centere
 d around the concept of "9 lives."</p><p>  The program showcases a range 
 of styles including contemporary\, modern\, jazz\, and experimental dance
 \, reflecting the diverse voices within the department. In addition to pe
 rformance\, the production emphasizes mentorship\, collaboration\, and pr
 ofessional development\, giving students hands-on experience in choreogra
 phy\, rehearsal process\, and live theater production.</p><p><a href="htt
 ps://www.srjcathletics.com/Athletic_Tickets" target="_blank" rel="noopene
 r">Buy tickets here!</a></p>
