BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Santa Rosa Junior College
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260512T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260512T130000
LOCATION:Frank Chong Black Box Theatre\, Burbank Auditorium - Santa Rosa 
 Campus
SUMMARY:Immigrant Pathways to Economic Mobility
DESCRIPTION:You are invited to attend the 2026 Del Monte Lecture hosted b
 y the SRJC Foundation.  "Immigrant Pathways to Economic Mobility - The Ro
 le of Education\, Workforce Development\, and Entrepreneurship"  This yea
 r's featured speaker\, Dr. Marlene Orozco\, is a nationally recognized re
 searcher in economic mobility\, entrepreneurship\, and equity. Her talk w
 ill connect national research with local impact\, highlighting how immigr
 ants contribute to Sonoma County's economy and the critical role SRJC pla
 ys in creating pathways through education\, career training\, and entrepr
 eneurship.  This lecture offers an opportunity to:  • Engage with resea
 rch that aligns with our work across instruction\, student services\, and
  workforce development  • Reflect on how our programs support economic 
 mobility and community vitality  • Connect with colleagues\, students\,
  and community partners around a shared topic of impact  The event is fre
 e and open to all\; we encourage you to attend.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  You are invited to attend the 2026 Del 
 Monte Lecture hosted by the SRJC Foundation.</p><p>  "Immigrant Pathways 
 to Economic Mobility - The Role of Education\, Workforce Development\, an
 d Entrepreneurship"</p><p>  This year's featured speaker\, Dr. Marlene Or
 ozco\, is a nationally recognized researcher in economic mobility\, entre
 preneurship\, and equity. Her talk will connect national research with lo
 cal impact\, highlighting how immigrants contribute to Sonoma County's ec
 onomy and the critical role SRJC plays in creating pathways through educa
 tion\, career training\, and entrepreneurship.<br />  This lecture offers
  an opportunity to:<br />  • Engage with research that aligns with our 
 work across instruction\, student services\, and workforce development<br
  />  • Reflect on how our programs support economic mobility and commun
 ity vitality<br />  • Connect with colleagues\, students\, and communit
 y partners around a shared topic of impact<br />  The event is free and o
 pen to all\; we encourage you to attend.</p>
